# Protocol baseline
#
# The upstream snapshot this client implementation is written against. Every
# protocol-layer change must be traceable to the version recorded here.
# Drift detection (scripts/drift-check.sh) reads this file.

UPSTREAM_REPO=NodePassProject/Nowhere
UPSTREAM_BRANCH=main
UPSTREAM_TAG=v1.8.0
UPSTREAM_COMMIT=7720311b
UPSTREAM_COMMIT_DATE=2026-08-24
BINARY_VERSION_STRING=nowhere-v1.8.0

# Normative files watched for change
SPEC_FILES=docs/protocol.md docs/configuration.md docs/compatibility.md docs/security.md

# Known state
# - v1.8.0 was released on 2026-08-24; the feat/mux branch was merged into main
#   and deleted. Compared with the feat/mux@820b0c5 snapshot this suite was first
#   built from, v1.8.0 differs only in the version number, Cargo.lock and one test
#   file - no normative file and no implementation code changed, so all earlier
#   analysis holds unchanged.
# - Relative to 1.7: adds the TLS Mux carrier; removes the pool parameter
#   (replaced by mux=0|1, default 0); drops the Linux-only gate and adds
#   cross-platform CI plus GHCR container images.
# - Authentication (spec section 2) and FlowHeader (section 4) are unchanged since
#   1.7, so the byte-level vectors carry across versions.
# - Verified: cargo build --release --locked succeeds on macOS/aarch64, and the
#   end-to-end smoke test passes against the resulting binary.
#
# Tracking policy (decided 2026-08-24)
#
# The baseline stays pinned at v1.8.0 for the whole of M0 and L1. It is NOT
# advanced just because upstream moved: a moving target during the first
# implementation of the protocol layer costs more than it buys, and the vectors
# in this suite were derived against exactly this snapshot.
#
# Upstream has already advanced past this pin (89750106 as of 2026-08-24) with
# no normative change. That is the expected steady state: drift-check.sh reports
# the distance and passes. Only a normative change - one of the SPEC_FILES above
# - should interrupt development, and it exits non-zero so a scheduled CI job can
# open an issue.
#
# Revisit the pin at the L1 exit, or immediately on a normative change.
#
# When advancing the baseline: run scripts/drift-check.sh first, then update this
# file, then re-run scripts/verify-vectors.py and scripts/smoke-local.sh.
